USER USER --------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER The export.rs module was refactored to use NixCryptoArgs from common.rs,
USER USER removing the duplicated store and logger resolution logic. The following
USER USER changes were made:
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.1 New IdentityType variant
USER USER 
USER USER     OpensslSymmetricKey {
USER USER         key_id: String,
USER USER         key_derivation: String,
USER USER         iterations: u32,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Added alongside the existing OpensslPkey variant to represent a symmetric key
USER USER identity for the export secret subcommand.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.2 OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity struct
USER USER 
USER USER A private struct implementing IsOpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity was defined locally
USER USER in export.rs:
USER USER 
USER USER     struct OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity {
USER USER         key_id: String,
USER USER         key_derivation: String,
USER USER         iterations: u32,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER This is used in run_secret to call crypto_nix.openssl_symmetric_key_passphrase.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.3 resolve_identity_type
USER USER 
USER USER The resolve_identity_type function was extended to handle the new
USER USER "openssl-symmetric-key" identity type. It reads the three new flags:
USER USER 
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-id (required)
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-derivation (optional, defaults to "pbkdf2")
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-iterations (optional, defaults to 600000)
USER USER 
USER USER The iterations flag is parsed as a u32, with a descriptive error returned if
USER USER the value is not a valid positive integer.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.4 resolve_args
USER USER 
USER USER The resolve_args function signature was updated to accept NixCryptoArgs instead
USER USER of individual store and logger flags, and to accept the three new symmetric key
USER USER flags.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.5 run_secret
USER USER 
USER USER The run_secret function was extended with a new match arm for
USER USER IdentityType::OpensslSymmetricKey. It:
USER USER 
USER USER   1. Constructs an OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity from the resolved fields.
USER USER   2. Calls crypto_nix.openssl_symmetric_key_passphrase to retrieve the
USER USER      passphrase from the store (or derive and store it on first use).
USER USER   3. Writes the passphrase as a plain string to the output file specified by
USER USER      --output-file.
USER USER   4. Prints a success message to stdout.
USER USER 
