USER USER 4. NIX LAYER CHANGES (crypto/openssl/)
USER USER ----------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER 4.1 crypto/openssl/export-decryptable-pkey-params-type.nix (new file)
USER USER -----------------------------------------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER A new NixOS module type was defined for the parameters of export-decryptable-pkey:
USER USER 
USER USER     types.submodule {
USER USER       options = {
USER USER         key-id = lib.mkOption { type = types.str; ... };
USER USER         key-derivation = lib.mkOption {
USER USER           type = types.enum [ "pbkdf2" ];
USER USER           default = "pbkdf2";
USER USER           ...
USER USER         };
USER USER         iterations = lib.mkOption { type = types.int; ... };
USER USER       };
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER This type enforces that callers provide a valid key-id, a supported
USER USER key-derivation scheme, and a positive integer number of iterations.
USER USER 
USER USER 4.2 crypto/openssl/default.nix
USER USER --------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER The new export-decryptable-pkey-params-type was registered in the module scope:
USER USER 
USER USER     export-decryptable-pkey-params-type =
USER USER       self.callPackage ./export-decryptable-pkey-params-type.nix {};
USER USER 
USER USER 4.3 crypto/openssl/main.nix
USER USER -----------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER The export-decryptable-pkey-params-type was added as a module argument.
USER USER 
USER USER A private helper function export-decryptable-pkey was defined:
USER USER 
USER USER     export-decryptable-pkey = { key-ref, symmetric-key-params }:
USER USER       openssl.export-decryptable-pkey symmetric-key-params key-ref
USER USER     ;
USER USER 
USER USER This calls the Nix primop openssl.export-decryptable-pkey with the symmetric
USER USER key params as the first argument and the private key reference as the second,
USER USER matching the arity-2 primop signature.
USER USER 
USER USER The export-decryptable-pkey function was exposed on the private key attribute
USER USER set returned by private-key-impl, wrapped in a type-checker.function call that
USER USER validates the symmetric-key-params argument against
USER USER export-decryptable-pkey-params-type:
USER USER 
USER USER     export-decryptable-pkey =
USER USER       type-checker.function
USER USER       [ { name = "symmetric-key-params";
USER USER           type = export-decryptable-pkey-params-type; } ]
USER USER       (symmetric-key-params:
USER USER         export-decryptable-pkey { inherit key-ref symmetric-key-params; })
USER USER     ;
USER USER 
USER USER The identity field was also added to the private key attribute set:
USER USER 
USER USER     identity = key-ref.key-identity;
USER USER 
USER USER This exposes the key identity string directly so that callers such as
USER USER nix-crypto-service can locate the key in the sled store without reconstructing
USER USER the identity manually.
USER USER 
USER USER 
USER USER 5. SERVICE CHANGES (nix-crypto-service)
USER USER -----------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1 Refactoring: nix-crypto-service/src/common.rs (new file)
USER USER --------------------------------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER As part of this session, shared CryptoNix initialisation logic was extracted
USER USER from export.rs into a new common.rs module. This module defines:
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.1 Error enum
USER USER 
USER USER     pub enum Error {
USER USER         ArgumentError(String),
USER USER         UnknownAction,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER A unified error type for the service crate. ArgumentError carries a descriptive
USER USER message. UnknownAction is returned when no recognised subcommand is matched.
USER USER The as_string method formats the error for display to the user.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.2 StoreArgs enum
USER USER 
USER USER     pub enum StoreArgs {
USER USER         SledStoreArgs { sled_store_directory: String },
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Represents the specification for initialising a credential store. Currently
USER USER only the Sled backend is supported. The resolve_sled_store associated function
USER USER resolves the store path from either the --sled-store CLI flag or the
USER USER NIX_CRYPTO_STORE environment variable (which must be in the format
USER USER "sled:<path>"). The to_config method converts StoreArgs into a SledModeConfig
USER USER for use with CryptoNix::from_sled_config.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.3 LogArgs struct
USER USER 
USER USER     pub struct LogArgs {
USER USER         pub log_file: Option<String>,
USER USER         pub log_level: Option<LogLevel>,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Represents the specification for initialising the logger. The from_flags
USER USER associated function parses the --log-file and --log-level CLI flags. The init
USER USER method constructs a Logger, returning Logger::dummy() if no log file is
USER USER specified, or Logger::file() otherwise. The log level defaults to LogLevel::Info
USER USER if absent.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.4 NixCryptoArgs struct
USER USER 
USER USER     pub struct NixCryptoArgs {
USER USER         pub nix_crypto_store: StoreArgs,
USER USER         pub nix_crypto_log: LogArgs,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Combines StoreArgs and LogArgs into a single struct that can be used to
USER USER initialise a CryptoNix instance. The from_flags associated function is the
USER USER primary constructor, accepting the three relevant CLI flags. The init method
USER USER calls nix_crypto_log.init() to obtain a Logger and nix_crypto_store.to_config()
USER USER to obtain a SledModeConfig, then calls CryptoNix::from_sled_config.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2 nix-crypto-service/src/export.rs
USER USER --------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER The export.rs module was refactored to use NixCryptoArgs from common.rs,
USER USER removing the duplicated store and logger resolution logic. The following
USER USER changes were made:
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.1 New IdentityType variant
USER USER 
USER USER     OpensslSymmetricKey {
USER USER         key_id: String,
USER USER         key_derivation: String,
USER USER         iterations: u32,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Added alongside the existing OpensslPkey variant to represent a symmetric key
USER USER identity for the export secret subcommand.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.2 OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity struct
USER USER 
USER USER A private struct implementing IsOpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity was defined locally
USER USER in export.rs:
USER USER 
USER USER     struct OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity {
USER USER         key_id: String,
USER USER         key_derivation: String,
USER USER         iterations: u32,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER This is used in run_secret to call crypto_nix.openssl_symmetric_key_passphrase.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.3 resolve_identity_type
USER USER 
USER USER The resolve_identity_type function was extended to handle the new
USER USER "openssl-symmetric-key" identity type. It reads the three new flags:
USER USER 
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-id (required)
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-derivation (optional, defaults to "pbkdf2")
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-iterations (optional, defaults to 600000)
USER USER 
USER USER The iterations flag is parsed as a u32, with a descriptive error returned if
USER USER the value is not a valid positive integer.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.4 resolve_args
USER USER 
USER USER The resolve_args function signature was updated to accept NixCryptoArgs instead
USER USER of individual store and logger flags, and to accept the three new symmetric key
USER USER flags.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.5 run_secret
USER USER 
USER USER The run_secret function was extended with a new match arm for
USER USER IdentityType::OpensslSymmetricKey. It:
USER USER 
USER USER   1. Constructs an OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity from the resolved fields.
USER USER   2. Calls crypto_nix.openssl_symmetric_key_passphrase to retrieve the
USER USER      passphrase from the store (or derive and store it on first use).
USER USER   3. Writes the passphrase as a plain string to the output file specified by
USER USER      --output-file.
USER USER   4. Prints a success message to stdout.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.3 nix-crypto-service/src/main.rs
USER USER ------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER The main.rs module was updated to:
USER USER 
USER USER   1. Declare the new common module and import NixCryptoArgs and Error from it.
USER USER   2. Add three new CLI flags to the USAGE string and Args struct:
USER USER        --openssl-symmetric-key-id
USER USER        --openssl-symmetric-key-derivation
USER USER        --openssl-symmetric-key-iterations
USER USER   3. Implement to_nix_crypto_args on Args, which calls NixCryptoArgs::from_flags
USER USER      with the sled store, log file, and log level flags.
USER USER   4. Move the subcommand dispatch logic into an Args::main method, which returns
USER USER      Result<(), Error> and is called from the top-level main function.
USER USER   5. Pass the three new symmetric key flags through to export::resolve_args.
USER USER 
USER USER 
USER USER 6. DATA FLOW SUMMARY
USER USER ---------------------
USER USER 
USER USER 6.1 Export Decryptable (Nix primop path)
USER USER 
USER USER   Nix code calls:
USER USER     private-key.export-decryptable-pkey { key-id = ...; key-derivation = ...;
USER USER                                            iterations = ...; }
USER USER 
USER USER   This calls the Nix primop:
USER USER     openssl.export-decryptable-pkey symmetric-key-params key-ref
USER USER 
USER USER   The primop (arity 2) is handled by primop_openssl_export_decryptable_pkey in
USER USER   openssl_primops.cc, which:
USER USER     1. Reads the symmetric key identity from args[0] via
USER USER        openssl_get_symmetric_key_identity.
USER USER     2. Reads the private key identity from args[1] via
USER USER        openssl_get_private_key_identity.
USER USER     3. Calls primops->opensslExportDecryptableOpensslPkey.
USER USER 
USER USER   CryptoNixPrimops::opensslExportDecryptableOpensslPkey delegates to:
USER USER     cryptoNix()->cxx_export_decryptable_openssl_pkey(symmetric_key, credential)
USER USER 
USER USER   CxxNixCrypto::cxx_export_decryptable_openssl_pkey calls:
USER USER     export_decryptable(&self.0, &symmetric_key,
USER USER                        &OpensslPrivateKeyIdentityWrapper(&credential))
USER USER 
USER USER   decryptable::export_decryptable:
USER USER     1. get_or_derive(SymmetricKeyIdentity(key)) -> SymmetricKeyValue
USER USER     2. get_or_derive(OpensslPrivateKeyIdentityWrapper(credential)) -> Key
USER USER     3. get_or_derive(EncryptionParamsKey(sym_id, cred)) -> EncryptionParams
USER USER     4. credential_value.export() -> Vec<u8> (PEM bytes of private key)
USER USER     5. encrypt_to_pem(sym_key_value, salt, iv, plaintext) -> PEM String
USER USER 
USER USER   The resulting PEM string is returned up the call stack and set as a Nix
USER USER   string value.
USER USER 
USER USER 6.2 Symmetric Key Passphrase Export (CLI path)
USER USER 
USER USER   User invokes:
USER USER     nix-crypto-service export secret \
USER USER       --identity-type openssl-symmetric-key \
USER USER       --openssl-symmetric-key-id <id> \
USER USER       --openssl-symmetric-key-derivation pbkdf2 \
USER USER       --openssl-symmetric-key-iterations 600000 \
USER USER       --output-file <path>
USER USER 
USER USER   Args::main calls export::resolve_args, which calls resolve_identity_type,
USER USER   producing IdentityType::OpensslSymmetricKey { key_id, key_derivation,
USER USER   iterations }.
USER USER 
USER USER   export::run_secret:
USER USER     1. Calls args.nix_crypto_args.init() to construct a CryptoNix instance.
USER USER     2. Constructs OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity { key_id, key_derivation,
USER USER        iterations }.
USER USER     3. Calls crypto_nix.openssl_symmetric_key_passphrase(&identity).
USER USER     4. Delegates to decryptable::get_symmetric_key_passphrase, which calls
USER USER        get_or_derive(SymmetricKeyIdentity(key)) and returns
USER USER        symmetric_key_value.random_secret.
USER USER     5. Writes the passphrase string to the output file.
USER USER 
USER USER 
USER USER 7. SECURITY NOTES
USER USER ------------------
USER USER 
USER USER   - The random_secret is generated using OpenSSL's rand_bytes, which is a
USER USER     cryptographically secure random number generator.
USER USER   - The random_secret is 16 bytes (128 bits) of entropy, base64-encoded to a
USER USER     24-character string.
USER USER   - The AES key is derived from random_secret using PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 with a
USER USER     configurable iteration count. The default is 600,000 iterations, which is
USER USER     consistent with current NIST recommendations for PBKDF2 with SHA-256.
USER USER   - A unique salt and IV are generated for each (symmetric_key, credential)
USER USER     pair and persisted in the store. This ensures that the same plaintext
USER USER     encrypted with the same key always produces the same ciphertext (required
USER USER     for Nix referential transparency), while preventing IV reuse across
USER USER     different (key, credential) pairs.
USER USER   - The passphrase (random_secret) written to disk by nix-crypto-service is
USER USER     sensitive. The caller is responsible for ensuring the output file has
USER USER     appropriate permissions.
USER USER   - Private keys are never exposed in the Nix language. The export-decryptable-pkey
USER USER     primop returns an encrypted PEM string, not the raw private key.
USER USER 
USER USER 
