USER USER 5. SERVICE CHANGES (nix-crypto-service)
USER USER -----------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1 Refactoring: nix-crypto-service/src/common.rs (new file)
USER USER --------------------------------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER As part of this session, shared CryptoNix initialisation logic was extracted
USER USER from export.rs into a new common.rs module. This module defines:
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.1 Error enum
USER USER 
USER USER     pub enum Error {
USER USER         ArgumentError(String),
USER USER         UnknownAction,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER A unified error type for the service crate. ArgumentError carries a descriptive
USER USER message. UnknownAction is returned when no recognised subcommand is matched.
USER USER The as_string method formats the error for display to the user.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.2 StoreArgs enum
USER USER 
USER USER     pub enum StoreArgs {
USER USER         SledStoreArgs { sled_store_directory: String },
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Represents the specification for initialising a credential store. Currently
USER USER only the Sled backend is supported. The resolve_sled_store associated function
USER USER resolves the store path from either the --sled-store CLI flag or the
USER USER NIX_CRYPTO_STORE environment variable (which must be in the format
USER USER "sled:<path>"). The to_config method converts StoreArgs into a SledModeConfig
USER USER for use with CryptoNix::from_sled_config.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.3 LogArgs struct
USER USER 
USER USER     pub struct LogArgs {
USER USER         pub log_file: Option<String>,
USER USER         pub log_level: Option<LogLevel>,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Represents the specification for initialising the logger. The from_flags
USER USER associated function parses the --log-file and --log-level CLI flags. The init
USER USER method constructs a Logger, returning Logger::dummy() if no log file is
USER USER specified, or Logger::file() otherwise. The log level defaults to LogLevel::Info
USER USER if absent.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.1.4 NixCryptoArgs struct
USER USER 
USER USER     pub struct NixCryptoArgs {
USER USER         pub nix_crypto_store: StoreArgs,
USER USER         pub nix_crypto_log: LogArgs,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Combines StoreArgs and LogArgs into a single struct that can be used to
USER USER initialise a CryptoNix instance. The from_flags associated function is the
USER USER primary constructor, accepting the three relevant CLI flags. The init method
USER USER calls nix_crypto_log.init() to obtain a Logger and nix_crypto_store.to_config()
USER USER to obtain a SledModeConfig, then calls CryptoNix::from_sled_config.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2 nix-crypto-service/src/export.rs
USER USER --------------------------------------
USER USER 
USER USER The export.rs module was refactored to use NixCryptoArgs from common.rs,
USER USER removing the duplicated store and logger resolution logic. The following
USER USER changes were made:
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.1 New IdentityType variant
USER USER 
USER USER     OpensslSymmetricKey {
USER USER         key_id: String,
USER USER         key_derivation: String,
USER USER         iterations: u32,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER Added alongside the existing OpensslPkey variant to represent a symmetric key
USER USER identity for the export secret subcommand.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.2 OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity struct
USER USER 
USER USER A private struct implementing IsOpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity was defined locally
USER USER in export.rs:
USER USER 
USER USER     struct OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity {
USER USER         key_id: String,
USER USER         key_derivation: String,
USER USER         iterations: u32,
USER USER     }
USER USER 
USER USER This is used in run_secret to call crypto_nix.openssl_symmetric_key_passphrase.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.3 resolve_identity_type
USER USER 
USER USER The resolve_identity_type function was extended to handle the new
USER USER "openssl-symmetric-key" identity type. It reads the three new flags:
USER USER 
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-id (required)
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-derivation (optional, defaults to "pbkdf2")
USER USER   - --openssl-symmetric-key-iterations (optional, defaults to 600000)
USER USER 
USER USER The iterations flag is parsed as a u32, with a descriptive error returned if
USER USER the value is not a valid positive integer.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.4 resolve_args
USER USER 
USER USER The resolve_args function signature was updated to accept NixCryptoArgs instead
USER USER of individual store and logger flags, and to accept the three new symmetric key
USER USER flags.
USER USER 
USER USER 5.2.5 run_secret
USER USER 
USER USER The run_secret function was extended with a new match arm for
USER USER IdentityType::OpensslSymmetricKey. It:
USER USER 
USER USER   1. Constructs an OpensslSymmetricKeyIdentity from the resolved fields.
USER USER   2. Calls crypto_nix.openssl_symmetric_key_passphrase to retrieve the
USER USER      passphrase from the store (or derive and store it on first use).
USER USER   3. Writes the passphrase as a plain string to the output file specified by
USER USER      --output-file.
USER USER   4. Prints a success message to stdout.
USER USER 
